        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T15:53:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "isntead of having this as a global, what you think about using `queue_peek_units(\u0026cmsis_dap_rx_queue, rx_buffer, 0, 5);` inline where you access `peek_c` now?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "a9d94b2c14aaacf4c432238f11d61b94dfd67794",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e67dac4_83836633",
        "filename": "board/hyperdebug/cmsis-dap.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T16:45:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do not know it is warranted, but my concern was performance.  If there is several levels of branching, it feels silly that cmsis_dap_deferred() would call queue_peek_units() to peek at one byte, and then call a handler method, which might peek at the second byte in order to branch internally, before some of the branches peeked at a little more data, in order to decide if the entire request has been received and can be processed.\n\nI could make peek_c a parameter to the handler methods, rather than a global variable (rx_buffer[] and tx_buffer[] would still be global, though.)",
      "parentUuid": "970a787f_8189713f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "a9d94b2c14aaacf4c432238f11d61b94dfd67794",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
