        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T16:45:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just thought that it was good to have \"room\" for more bitfields.  But thinking about it, since we have an explicit length byte in the response, it is easy to add more bits, or other structured data fields in the future, in a way that allows older clients to safely ignore the added fields.  I do not need to make it four bytes from the start.",
      "parentUuid": "70d1f5cd_f9efd8d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 233,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "a9d94b2c14aaacf4c432238f11d61b94dfd67794",
